      "note": "<p>PROVISIONAL Codex English-first proposal. The bracketed explanation after <i>second part</i> supplies its topic and is not assigned to <code>gnyis pa</code>. The first English <i>foundation consciousness</i> and <i>mental seeds</i> occur inside that supplied bracket; <i>Suppose</i> and <i>Nonetheless</i> advance the English cursor so the Tibetan terms select their actual occurrences in the argument. Articles, <i>you</i>, <i>the existence of</i>, passive <i>get</i>/<i>been</i>, and repeated complementizer <i>that</i> remain unwrapped.</p><p>The modal predicate is split without over-capture: <code>dgos</code> owns <i>must</i> and <code>'dod</code> owns <i>accept</i>. In the quotation, the title and beginningless-time compound keep only contained members; <i>For</i>, <i>in</i>, passive auxiliaries, <i>by people</i>, and emphatic <i>themselves</i> remain English additions. Each <code>dngos po</code> and <code>bag chags</code> occurrence is selected after an independent cursor anchor. The later sentence's missing quotation noun is not manufactured: <code>de 'dra ba</code>, <code>gzhan</code>, and <code>mang du</code> own only <i>same thing</i>, <i>other</i>, and <i>many</i>; <i>quotations which mention</i> is left unwrapped, and the distributed <code>'byung ba'i phyir ro</code> is omitted rather than nulled.</p><p>The first final <code>gzhi</code> is banked once as <i>basis</i>, leaving its synonymous repeated <i>or place</i> unwrapped; the second selects the later <i>place</i> after <i>What ... this</i>. The copular/question frame <code>yin zhe na</code> is recast as <i>provides</i> with supplied participants and is omitted. Exact C16 repetition and differing ILL parallels establish no source correction; no erratum is proposed.</p>"
